{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02956",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.63,
      "end_seconds": 6.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Uh, doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.41,
      "end_seconds": 11.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.79,
      "end_seconds": 27.04,
      "duration_seconds": 14.25,
      "text": "Yeah, it's a severe headache. I don't know what's causing it. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.84,
      "end_seconds": 32.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.58,
      "end_seconds": 36.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I've had it since last weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.15,
      "end_seconds": 46.88,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.06,
      "end_seconds": 63.65,
      "duration_seconds": 15.59,
      "text": "Honestly, all the time. I'd call it moderate. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.05,
      "end_seconds": 67.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.9,
      "end_seconds": 80.99,
      "duration_seconds": 12.09,
      "text": "Pain under the right ribs goes along with it, most of the time. The pain under the right ribs? That's been for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.59,
      "end_seconds": 94.84,
      "duration_seconds": 10.25,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.75,
      "end_seconds": 104.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.1,
      "text": "Maybe a three out of ten on a bad day. It happens once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.3,
      "end_seconds": 109.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.36,
      "end_seconds": 120.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.7,
      "end_seconds": 145.22,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 157 over 92, respiratory rate 16, temperature 36.7, oxygen saturation is 96 percent, pulse 81."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.45,
      "end_seconds": 148.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.53,
      "end_seconds": 153.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.27,
      "end_seconds": 159.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.57,
      "end_seconds": 161.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.48,
      "end_seconds": 175.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Your blood pressure is very high and your reflexes are brisk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.16,
      "end_seconds": 182.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "That's the examination finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.12,
      "end_seconds": 200.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Have you had any vaginal bleeding, reduced baby movements or leaking fluid?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.56,
      "end_seconds": 212.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "I, I haven't had vaginal bleeding, reduced baby movements or leaking fluid, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.22,
      "end_seconds": 216.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.46,
      "end_seconds": 223.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Well, no, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.04,
      "end_seconds": 228.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.31,
      "end_seconds": 232.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.29,
      "end_seconds": 245.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.01,
      "end_seconds": 250.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Eczema, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.49,
      "end_seconds": 253.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.62,
      "end_seconds": 256.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.27,
      "end_seconds": 260.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.53,
      "end_seconds": 264.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I'm on hydrocortisone cream, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.57,
      "end_seconds": 268.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.02,
      "end_seconds": 281.19,
      "duration_seconds": 11.17,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. I grab fast food at lunch most days. I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.55,
      "end_seconds": 291.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.25,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, it's hard to say. Severe pre-eclampsia is one possibility and a migraine another, and I'd rather not commit yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.82,
      "end_seconds": 295.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.95,
      "end_seconds": 302.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like severe pre-eclampsia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.91,
      "end_seconds": 329.93,
      "duration_seconds": 11.02,
      "text": "For this, labetalol, 200 milligrams, once now, single dose. That's for severe hypertension. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.23,
      "end_seconds": 336.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.01,
      "end_seconds": 339.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}